  <!-- ══ 9. VOTING DAY ══ -->
  <div class="wp-section" id="s9">
    <h2><span class="sec-num">09</span> Voting Day: From Ballot to Tally</h2>

    <h3>9.1 Voter Authentication</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Step 1 &mdash; Open BonID App:</strong> Voter launches the BonID mobile application.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 2 &mdash; Liveness Verification:</strong> Biometric face match + liveness detection confirms the physical person.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 3 &mdash; Eligibility Check:</strong> API verifies BonID is verified, CIN is on voter roll, nullifier check confirms voter hasn't voted yet, geolocation noted.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 4 &mdash; Ballot Routing:</strong> Based on BonID location code (4th segment), voter receives the correct ballot: domestic (3 sections) or diaspora (1 section).</li>
      <li><strong>Step 5 &mdash; Vote on Device:</strong> Voter selects candidates. The app generates Schnorr ZKP proof, Pedersen commitment, AES-256-GCM encryption, nullifier, and ballot hash.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 6 &mdash; Cast:</strong> Encrypted ballot sent to server. Server stores the encrypted blob without ever seeing the vote. Voter receives a ballot_hash receipt.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>9.2 What the Server Stores (per ballot)</h3>
    <div class="wp-table-wrap">
      <table class="wp-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Content</th><th>Reveals Vote?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>nullifier</td><td>SHA-256 hash (unique per voter per election)</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>encrypted_choice</td><td>AES-256-GCM encrypted blob + IV + auth_tag</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>encrypted_key</td><td>RSA-encrypted AES session key</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>zkp_commitment</td><td>Pedersen commitment hiding the vote</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>zkp_proof</td><td>Schnorr proof (challenge, response, public_commitment)</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ballot_hash</td><td>SHA-256 of entire ballot (voter receipt)</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>receipt_id</td><td>Unique public identifier</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>channel</td><td>remote / consulate / in_person</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>department_code</td><td>From BonID location code</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ip_country</td><td>From IP geolocation (cached)</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>cast_at</td><td>Timestamp</td><td style="color:var(--ht-green); font-weight:700;">No</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #64748B; font-style: italic;">The server stores 11 fields per ballot. None of them reveal the voter's choice.</p>

    <h3>9.3 Performance</h3>
